n Si Thammarat Province but the elevation is unknown. Its presence on Ko Tao Island, Surat Thani Province, approximately 85 km off the coast from Muang District, Chumpon Province, as opposed to the presence of Cnemaspis siamensis which is geographically closer to Ko Tao Island, is consistent with the geological history of this part of Peninsular Thailand. The island chain consisting of Ko Tao and the intervening islands Ko Samui and Ko Phangan, are offshore extensions of the Nakhon Si Thammarat Mountains to which they were connected during the last glacial maximum (Sathiamurthy & Voris 2006) and lie to the east of the Isthmus of Kra. It is likely that C. chanardi also occurs on Ko Samui and Ko Phangan; see also map [Fig. 1] in GRISMER et al. 2010)","","text","",""]]},"WGL2":{"v":[["Dring’s Rock Gecko","eng",0],["Dring's Day Gecko","eng",0],["Sarawak Round-eyed Gecko","eng",0]],"d":[["Indonesia, Malaysia (Borneo)","","text","",""]]},"XHFV":{"v":[["חד-צלע חלק","heb",0],["利氏秀殺牛蠍","zho",0]]},"XHG5":{"v":[["淡色秀殺牛蠍","zho",0]]},"3232R":{"d":[["VC","VC","iso","",""],["WIN-BA","WIN-BA","tdwg","",""]]},"34NTS":{"d":[["","MOL","tdwg","",""]]},"35KWR":{"d":[["Gabon","","text","",""]]},"35SGZ":{"d":[["China (Guangdong).","","text","",""],["Oriental","","text","",""]]},"35SH9":{"d":[["Guatemala.","","text","",""],["Neotropic","","text","",""]]},"362GZ":{"d":[["","NWG-PN","tdwg","native",""],["Papua New Guinea","","text","native",""]]},"362H9":{"d":[["","AR","iso","native",""],["Argentina","","text","native",""]]},"394ZB":{"d":[["Kerala","","text","",""],["Tamil Nadu","","text","",""]]},"398RF":{"d":[["","CMN-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","GAB-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","LBR-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","NGA-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","ZAI-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Cameroon, Gabon, Liberia, Nigeria, Zaire, French Congo","","text","native",""]]},"39GSV":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"3BKPL":{"d":[["Danish Exclusive Economic Zone","5674","mrgid","",""]]},"3BVYX":{"d":[[""